    pnp lbcert: sibling transfer service, monotone-equals-general family
    
    - relay op `sibling` (patch_relay2.py; handler on marceline-dev): prove a held step with a merged
      same-skeleton theorem (statement swap, consistent numeral remap), compiled against current upstream.
      Corpus test: 7 of 14 tried pairs compiled, most < 40 s. autosolve retries it every 5 min per held step.
    - monotone-equals-general family (83 open steps): exact general complexity by lb_cert plus an explicit
      AND/OR circuit of that size; routed through the lb-cert op (marceline monofam.py, compiled first).
      L-meta-8680 published end to end by the fast lane (PR 12919).
    - lbparse.family(); fastlane treats both families as concrete.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
